<title>USA: CIT Group sells $200 mln in notes.</title>
<headline>CIT Group sells $200 mln in notes.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following debt issue from CIT Group Holdings Inc was reoffered on Thursday, according to lead manager Salomon Brothers.</p>
<p>Salomon won the notes by competitive bid. Details of the bid were not disclosed.</p>
<p>CIT Group is a consumer finance company 80 percent owned by Dai-Ichi Kangyo Bank Ltd and 20 percent owned by Chase Manhattan Corp.</p>
<p>BORROWER CIT GROUP HOLDINGS INC</p>
<p>AMT $200 MLN	 COUPON 6.20 PCT    MATURITY 6/17/1999</p>
<p>TYPE NOTES	   ISS PRICE 100.00   FIRST PAY DATE 12/17/97</p>
<p>LAST MOODY'S Aa3   YIELD 6.20 PCT     PAY FREQ SEMI-ANNUAL</p>
<p>S&amp;P A-PLUS	   SPREAD 14 BPS	CALLABLE NO</p>
<p>((U.S. Corporate Bond Unit, 212-859-1672))</p>
</text>
